# LeakSanitizer suppressions for known upstream MuPDF leaks.
#
# Every entry here must name an upstream defect with a reproducer under
# tests/crashes/. Never suppress a leak in Leht's own code -- fix it.

# pdf_save_document with do_garbage >= 2 leaks ~874 bytes per call in the object
# renumbering path (renumberobj -> pdf_copy_dict -> pdf_new_dict). Confirmed in
# both MuPDF 1.28.2 and 1.28.4 with a pure-C reproducer containing no Leht code:
# tests/crashes/mupdf_save_leak_repro.c. Leaks scale linearly with saves.
#
# Leht keeps do_garbage=3 deliberately: de-duplication is worth far more than
# 874 bytes, since merging N similar files without it costs N copies of their
# shared fonts. See tests/crashes/README.md.
leak:renumberobj
leak:renumberobjs

# NOTE on libFuzzer: these suppressions only match when the stack can be
# symbolized, which needs llvm-symbolizer (Fedora package `llvm`). Without it
# libFuzzer reports the known upstream save leak as a finding and stops on the
# first corpus entry. Run libFuzzer with -detect_leaks=0 in that case; leak
# checking is covered properly by the GCC ASan build, where it works.
